==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|tick|er}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɪkə(ɹ)/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-ticker.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪkə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who makes a tick mark.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1992|title=Parliamentary Debates (Hansard)
|passage=A teacher now is a typist, a printer, a laboratory assistant, a designer of work sheets and booklets, a form-filler, a '''ticker''' of boxes and a sender of returns to faculty heads, to head teachers, to education authorities and to the Ministers {{...}}}}
# A measuring or reporting device, particularly one which makes a [[tick]]ing sound as the measured events occur.
#: {{ux|en|The '''ticker''' was showing an increased rate of flow.}}
# A [[ticker tape]], either the traditional paper kind or a scrolling message on a screen.
#: {{ux|en|I checked the prices on the '''ticker''' one last time before placing the trade.}}
#: {{ux|en|To my surprise, the '''ticker''' showed that the deal had already gone through.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A heart, especially a human one.
#: {{ux|en|My '''ticker''' gave out and I had to go to the hospital for surgery.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[watch]] {{gl|timepiece}}.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2011|author=Maggie MacKeever|title=The Tyburn Waltz
|passage=A right nice '''ticker''' it was. Real gold.}}
# {{lb|en|birdwatching|slang}} A [[birdwatcher]] who aims to see (and tick off on a list) as many bird species as possible.
# A [[beer]] [[drinker]] who aims to try as many different beers as possible and keeps a [[record]] of all the beers they have drunk.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=Richard Stedman|title=The Football and Real Ale Guide 2006-07: Division 1|isbn=9781905423071|url=https://www.google.co.uk/books/edition/Football_and_Real_Ale_Guide_06_07_Divisi/HxQt0g_X7u4C|page=5|text=My weekday visit found a great mix of luncheoners, locals and real ale '''tickers'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015|author=Max Bahnson|title=Prague: A Pisshead's Pub Guide|isbn=9781326456726|url=https://www.google.co.uk/books/edition/Prague_A_Pisshead_s_Pub_Guide_2nd_Editio/0fLXCgAAQBAJ|page=5|text=This book has not been written with the goal of pleasing beer geeks, '''tickers''', fetishists, raters or advocates.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019|author=Michael Ian Borer|title=Vegas Brews: Craft Beer and the Birth of a Local Scene|isbn=9781479885251|url=https://www.google.co.uk/books/edition/Vegas_Brews/Vx2yDwAAQBAJ|page=168|text=Today's '''tickers''' are equipped with smartphones with downloaded apps like Untappd. I've seen '''tickers''' peruse beer lists for new beers they haven't tried.}}

